---
title: 'Financial Charts - Volume Profile'
enterprise: true
---

A Volume Profile shows the traded volume at each price level alongside the price series.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Volume Profile" name="volume-profile" type="generated" /%}

## Volume Profile Chart

Use `AgCharts.createVolumeProfileChart()` to show a Volume Profile on its own, against a price axis.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Volume Profile Chart" name="volume-profile-chart" type="generated" /%}

## Total Segment

Set `totalSegment.enabled` to show a column between the price axis and the bars, with a block at each price level labelled with the total volume traded at that price. The series area narrows to make room for it, in the same way as it does for an axis.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Total Segment" name="total-segment" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    tickSize: 5,
    totalSegment: {
        enabled: true,
    },
}
```

In this example:

- Totals are abbreviated with a suffix, such as `1.2K` or `3.4M`. Supply a `label.formatter` to show them differently.
- The column is as wide as its widest label, but never narrower than `minWidth` (60 pixels by default). Set `width` to fix the width instead, in which case labels that do not fit are shortened.
- Price levels with no volume have no block, and labels are hidden when the price levels are too close together to read.

## Selecting Price Levels

Set `selection.enabled` to let users click a price level to select it, highlighting both its up and down segments and the background behind it. In a Financial Chart, set the same options on `volumeProfile.selection`.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Selecting Price Levels" name="selection" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    tickSize: 5,
    selection: {
        enabled: true,
        enableDrag: true,
    },
}
```

In this example:

- Click a price level to select it, or click away from the bars to clear the selection.
- With `enableDrag` set, drag across the chart to select every price level the rectangle touches.
- Use the Click Mode buttons to switch `selection.clickMode` between `'single'`, where each click replaces the selection, and `'multiple'`, where each click toggles a level.
